From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: avoid EN7523 LAN FAQ profile on AN7563

EN7523 uses 2 KiB HWFWD payload buffers on QDMA0, while AN7563 uses
1 KiB buffers on both QDMA instances.  Do not apply the EN7523 CDM1
FAQ configuration to the AN7563 LAN path because its thresholds describe
the 2 KiB buffer layout.

Keep the existing CDM2 configuration unchanged to avoid perturbing the
working AN7563 WAN path.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -6107,13 +6107,16 @@ static int airoha_fe_init(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 	airoha_fe_crsn_qsel_init(eth);
 
 	/* Match the EN7523 QDMA buffer layout used by the vendor firmware.
-	 * QDMA0/LAN has 32 MiB for 16K 2 KiB payloads, while QDMA1/WAN has
-	 * 16 MiB for 16K 1 KiB payloads.  FAQ thresholds must follow the
-	 * payload size selected for the corresponding QDMA.
+	 * Its QDMA0/LAN has 32 MiB for 16K 2 KiB payloads. AN7563 uses
+	 * 1 KiB payloads on both QDMAs, so do not apply that CDM1 profile.
 	 */
-	if (airoha_is(eth, airoha_en7523, airoha_an7563)) {
+	if (airoha_is(eth, airoha_en7523)) {
 		airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_CDM_FAQ_CFG(1), 0x07c7);
 		airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_CDM_FAQ_THR_CFG(1), 0xc40007f0);
+	}
+
+	/* Preserve the established 1 KiB QDMA1/WAN FAQ profile. */
+	if (airoha_is(eth, airoha_en7523, airoha_an7563)) {
 		airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_CDM_FAQ_CFG(2), 0x07e7);
 		airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_CDM_FAQ_THR_CFG(2), 0xc40003f0);
 	}
-- 
